17592186045417] [17592186284304 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d537aae5-2a22-587e-b62f-7a17ec56d1f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284480 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284480 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164397" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284480 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284480 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7}=1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284480 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed51767d-9824-5d39-b6b6-e61b0eec9664" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284480 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ 8-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =7 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =49 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ y & =-1\\pm 7 \\\\ y & =-8,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=-8$ and $y=6$ in the $yz$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284486 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284486 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164415" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284486 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284486 #edb/ref 1071 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2}=10$ and the plane $z=5$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9fe7c1c-a0c0-5194-ad34-b26b4e46d994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284486 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=5,$ we substitute $z=5$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+6)^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284487 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186283994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284487 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284487 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284487 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284487 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9ff5d288-247e-5774-82fd-1ca9271248d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284487 #edb/ref 1074 "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(3,-6).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284488 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284488 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284488 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284488 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the parabolic cylinder $(x-1)^{2}=3y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b95d118-b433-55d2-98f9-256c4ab46ffd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284488 #edb/ref 1074 "The full expression describing all points on our parabolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}=3y,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:(x-1)^{2}=3y\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is an upward-opening parabola with a vertex at $(1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17